Prism Deck contract — API 1.5.1 (2026-10-15). Stable for others to build on: the facet schema (src/facets/schema.js: surfaces key / span / strip / screen / deck, galleries themes · icons · motion · spans · dials · screens · apps), the render + slicing API (src/render.js: render(facet, opts) → { svg, keys, segments, widgets, screen }), the scene API (src/scene/index.js: surface(ctx) with background / glyph / text roles, compose / keyInto, SVG builder, shapes, Inter text-as-paths, OKLCH color, easing, seeded noise; the deck SVG subset in src/scene/validate.js), the glyph contract (src/glyphs/_glyph.js: 48-unit grid, safe area 6–42, roles line / fill / accent / dim / spark, states → tones, t-driven motion), the theme contract (src/themes/_theme.js: palette per mode, role styles, type, tones, background / surface / paint / paintGlyph / press / glyphBox / text, per-glyph overrides, helpers incl. pixelate), and the device registry (src/devices.js, generated from research/devices.json: 31 models incl. Galleon 100 SD, Stream Deck + and + XL). Read docs/authoring.md (the contract), docs/devices.md and docs/ASSIGNMENTS.md. Exemplars: theme `prism` (provisional; Lead Designer owns its art direction), 8 glyphs (play-pause, mic, volume, cpu, power, broadcast, clock, bulb) and 19 facets across all 7 galleries. Conformance: `npm test` (core + every facet × theme × mode × target; per gallery: `node --test --test-name-pattern="facet <gallery>/" test/facets.test.js`). Contact sheets: aaa-prism-ds/deck/shots/device-galleon-plus-mk2-xl-mini-theme-prism.png, sheet-icons-dark.png, sheet-icons-light.png. Breaking changes from here on bump API_VERSION in index.js and are announced in this file.

Changes (additive except the 1.4 Galleon widget geometry, nothing renamed or removed):
1.1 — tokens are now generated from design/tokens.json (npm run sync-tokens) and the prism theme implements the published deck key grammar (spectral index, off/on/alert/busy/disabled); new tone `busy`; theme.spectral(h, { tier: vivid | ink | wash }) and theme.ink(h) read the 12 token stops; surface metrics gain k.m.bleed (4@72) and k.m.text (8@72, text safe area); text roles accept a `baseline` (distance from the bottom, @72 units) in theme `type`; BASE type is micro 8 / value 600 (nothing below 8 px @72); glyphs may declare a natural `hue`; Inter 400/600/700 are real faces (src/scene/fonts/index.js).
1.2 — per-slice culling: render() slices of span / deck / strip / Galleon-widget surfaces keep only the elements whose conservative bounds touch the slice plus the defs they reference (src/scene/cull.js), so a key whose pixels didn't change is byte-identical frame to frame (runtimes: dedupe per key and send only changed keys); `cull: false` restores whole-canvas slices; per-slice budget 96 KB (aim for 32 KB). New `ctx.pressKey` (runtimes pass `opts.pressKey`, the pressed device key index) for span and deck facets. Backward compatible: same render() shape and options.
1.3 — context gains `pressedFor` (seconds held, 0 when released), `turnAge` (seconds since the last dial rotate) and `touch` ({ x, y, hold, age } on + / + XL strips; undefined on the Galleon and on keys); runtimes pass opts.pressedFor / opts.turnAge / opts.touch. Themes' paintGlyph(k, pen, { tone, box, styleOf }) now receives the glyph box. Culling is ~5–10× faster (clip-rect bounds for composed keys, memoized path bounds). Compact arc flags ("a5 5 0 0110 10") are rejected everywhere — validator, geom.parsePath and therefore src/raster — and the validator flags <g> inside <clipPath>. Cull bounds use exact arc extents (geom.arcBounds), not the radius disk. package.json exports ./raster and has a raster:goldens script. prism: crit breathes every 0.6 s. strip-refraction runs at 5 fps (encoder feedback budget).
1.3.1 — culling is strict (an element whose box only touches a slice edge — compose()'s exact clip of a neighbor — is left out); DATA_KEYS gains mic, camera, volume, and facets' optional `dataShape` passes through to the catalog; every theme preview shows the real Galleon dashboard on the screen; the λ label (theme.lambda / lambdaOf) reads the design tokens' 12 stops (296° → λ 436, rose → "494c"); catalog usage.code for theme facets names their own theme.
1.4 — hardware compatibility (aaa-prism-ds/hardware-lab): toDeviceSvg(svg) (src/scene/qt.js, exported from index.js and scene) prepares every frame for the Stream Deck app's Qt renderer — clipPath → equivalent luminance mask (the app ignores clipPath), preserveAspectRatio dropped, root aspect = viewBox; plugins call it right before setImage / setFeedback (data: URLs only). validateSvg(svg, { profile: 'device' }) checks device frames (masks allowed, clipPath flagged). Galleon widgets are 2:1: render().widgets are 360 × 180 windows centered in the 360 × 192 quadrants (x = dial·360, y = layer·192 + 6; 6 px gutters) and now carry { x, y, w, h }; the galleon-widget target is 360 × 180; deviceLayout() matches; D5's Galleon screens lay their panels into those windows. Complexity budget: every app frame (key, dial segment, Galleon widget, info bar) stays under 300 elements after toDeviceSvg — enforced by the conformance test; layered() merges soft halo entries by paint. Touch semantics documented (segment-local tapPos, hold: true, no swipes). Apps gallery gains a Controls category (meeting, scene and media keys); app-cpu-ring draws through theme roles / tones (monochrome themes stay monochrome); the Inter subset gains − (U+2212).
1.5 — stateful facets: an optional facet `game` block { init({ seed, device, grid, params }) → JSON state, reduce(state, event) → state (pure), tickHz ≤ 4 + ticking(state), animate } and ctx.game / ctx.gamePrev / ctx.gameEvent (last event + age). src/scene/game.js: createGameHost(facet, opts) → { state, dispatch, reset, pump, needsTick, fps, renderOpts, snapshot } (events press / release / rotate / touch / tick / reset, with cell / col / row added for keys), replayGame, the state-carried rng (rngSeed / rngNext / rngInt / rngShuffle), GAME_STATE_MAX 4 KB, GAME_FPS 12, GAME_RESET_HOLD_S 1.5; all exported from index.js. Surfaces gain paintPen(pen, o) / pictogram(draw, o) (custom pieces painted like glyphs). New gallery `games` (coral 34.2; Puzzles · Chance · Reflex · Board) with game-lights-out (any grid, solvable boards from the seed, levels) and game-dice (one key, 1–2 dice, roll animation from the event age). Hosted by the web player (press / release / dial push / rotate / strip touch → dispatch, hold 1.5 s → new game, opts.onGame for persistence, renders only during transitions or ticks) and the hid runner (same hook, no hold-reset on the Galleon); docs/game-runtime.md is the plugin integration note. The catalog's facet records carry `game` ({ tickHz, animate, reset }) or null.
1.5.1 — span / deck / slice geometry is rounded to 2 decimals in devices.js (r2, GEOM_DECIMALS) and the validator compares sizes at that precision (a + XL 3-row span is 398.66 everywhere; game-tictactoe runs on the + XL again); render() of deck facets on the Galleon returns `widgets` (4 × 360 × 180, x / y in the panel) like screen facets; ctx.heldFor (seconds the last finished press lasted; runtimes pass opts.heldFor — web player and hid runner do; game release events carry it); facets may set `still` (thumbnail instant; stillTime() and the catalog honor it); the spans gallery accepts deck surfaces (walls onto the + strip and the Galleon screen); text opacity (k.label / value / … { opacity }) fades the theme's whole lettering as one (shadow / halo / plate copies included — chrome's shadow ignored it) and textPath's faux-bold stroke fades with its fill; shoot.mjs --slices places every culled, device-ready slice as its own image (what the hardware gets); scene/scheduler.js createChangeGovernor caps a unit's fps by the keys its frames actually change. span-power-on is the boot sequence: runtimes play it once at start (replay: false, t from start) — docs/game-runtime.md § 7.
